       8,144 bytes. 48 bytes free. No padding.
       One HTML file. No downloaded assets.
       WebGL2 / Web Audio / Windows Edge or Chrome.
       1920 x 1080, fitted to the display.
       112 seconds. 72 bars of 7/8 at 135 BPM.

       THE FIRST PHOTON
         a pearl opens into a turbine of metallic leaves
       A FIELD OF HOURS
         copper tides carry a luminous cyan shoreline
       TORSION
         two sheets turn around a suspended golden spine
       THE CLOCK WITHOUT HANDS
         seven eccentric orbits keep their own time
       WRITING WITH LIGHT
         a continuous pen ties a knot in three dimensions
       THE SUN UNFOLDS
         a living instrument gathers its scattered parts
       AFTERIMAGE
         every leaf returns to the first photon

       ----------------------------------------------
       RUN
       ----------------------------------------------

       Double-click intro.html. Wait, then click or
       press Enter / Space. P pauses music and picture.
       Esc leaves fullscreen. Click to replay at end.
       Headphones recommended.

       Everything is generated before playback.
       No server, flags or network connection needed.

       ----------------------------------------------
       SOUND
       ----------------------------------------------

       A new score, written for this production:
       3+2+2 broken percussion, struck inharmonic metal,
       felt strings, moving extended harmonies, bowed
       voices, a five-note ostinato and reed counterline.
       Echoes at three and five eighth notes.

       5,376,000 stereo frames synthesized on the GPU.
       48 kHz. Integer timing. Audio-clock camera sync.

       ----------------------------------------------
       PICTURE
       ----------------------------------------------

       Bent polar leaves, tidal lamellae, double helicoid,
       eccentric clockwork and projected light writing.
       Soft shadows, AO, iridescence, brushed highlights,
       real plinth reflections, caustic interference,
       depth blur, bloom, edge smoothing and film grain.

